{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GB8phKp6iiS345jVv3oaAW","type":"tool_result","content":"README.md\nconfig.py\nlogs/connect-attempt.log\nlogs/support-tickets.md\nnotes/badges-for-your-users-achievements.md\nnotes/collecting-leads-with-apps-script.md\nnotes/intervals-icu-oauth-quirks-no-refresh-token-duplicate-scope.md\nserver.py\nstatic/app.js\nstatic/index.html\n\n### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n\n## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n\n> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n> Safari and Chrome.\n\nReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\nweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\ngotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n\n## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n\n> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n\nChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\nlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\nbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\nsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\nIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\nathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n`connect-attempt.log`).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8be47a90-2f7b-4aee-aba8-b973aef40035","uuid":"01c0151a-083d-4f85-9066-169cbede9ce5","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:48:38.602Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"README.md\nconfig.py\nlogs/connect-attempt.log\nlogs/support-tickets.md\nnotes/badges-for-your-users-achievements.md\nnotes/collecting-leads-with-apps-script.md\nnotes/intervals-icu-oauth-quirks-no-refresh-token-duplicate-scope.md\nserver.py\nstatic/app.js\nstatic/index.html\n\n### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n\n## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n\n> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n> Safari and Chrome.\n\nReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\nweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\ngotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n\n## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n\n> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n\nChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\nlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\nbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\nsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\nIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\nathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n`connect-attempt.log`).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GB8phKp6iiS345jVv3oaAW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEPCEAHTRrHBemNsXzMJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UKvcvyUdqFvJYLGJatcvH8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-ihBPDM; cat README.md config.py server.py static/app.js static/index.html; cat notes/intervals*"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2006,"cache_read_input_tokens":20035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2006},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8be47a90-2f7b-4aee-aba8-b973aef40035","uuid":"2d1512c4-64ca-4ea6-85a9-c652ed930e73","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:48:41.137Z","request_id":"req_011CgEPCDuQaFucHCNMYhgof","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UKvcvyUdqFvJYLGJatcvH8":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-ihBPDM; cat README.md config.py server.py static/app.js static/index.html; cat notes/intervals*"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UKvcvyUdqFvJYLGJatcvH8","type":"tool_result","content":"# tricoach\n\nBackend + single-page app for a small triathlon coaching practice. Coaches\nplan the week; athletes see it and connect their Intervals.icu account so the\napp can read wellness data and push planned workouts to their calendar. The\nathlete signs in to tricoach (token in `localStorage`, sent as\n`Authorization: Bearer` by the SPA's fetch wrapper), then clicks\n\"Connect Intervals.icu\", which runs the OAuth flow against Intervals.\n\n`server.py` is stdlib only (`python3 server.py`, port 8766) and keeps\neverything in memory; the shape is the same as the Postgres tables in prod.\nDev sign-in tokens: `tok-okafor` (default in the SPA) and `tok-rivera`.\n`config.py` holds the OAuth client placeholders. `logs/` has what we captured\nwhile looking into the connection problems.\nimport os\n\nPORT = 8766\nAPP_SECRET = \"dev-only-change-me-7c1f0a\"          # signs the OAuth state parameter\n\n# Intervals.icu OAuth client (placeholders; the real pair is in the deploy env)\nINTERVALS_BASE = os.environ.get(\"INTERVALS_BASE\", \"https://intervals.icu\")\nCLIENT_ID = \"tricoach-dev\"\nCLIENT_SECRET = \"s3cr3t-placeholder-0000\"\nREDIRECT_URI = f\"http://localhost:{PORT}/api/intervals/callback\"\nSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"\n\nREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"tricoach backend: sign-in, Intervals.icu OAuth connection, wellness proxy.\n\nStdlib only. State is in memory (same shape as the prod tables).\n\"\"\"\nimport base64, hashlib, hmac, json, os, threading, time\nimport urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n\nimport config\n\nSTATIC = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \"static\")\nTOKEN_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/api/oauth/token\"\nAUTHORIZE_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/oauth/authorize\"\nDEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n\n# --- in-memory store -------------------------------------------------------\nUSERS = {\n    \"tok-okafor\": {\"id\": \"u_okafor\", \"name\": \"C. Okafor\"},\n    \"tok-rivera\": {\"id\": \"u_rivera\", \"name\": \"T. Rivera\"},\n}\n# user_id -> {athlete_id, athlete_name, access_token, refresh_token, scope, expires_at, status}\nCONNECTIONS = {}\nLOCK = threading.Lock()\n\n\ndef log(msg):\n    print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[intervals]\", msg, flush=True)\n\n\n# --- state parameter: carries the user through the redirect -----------------\ndef sign_state(user_id):\n    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}\"\n    sig = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(f\"{payload}:{sig}\".encode()).decode()\n\n\ndef verify_state(state, max_age=900):\n    try:\n        user_id, ts, sig = base64.urlsafe_b64decode(state.encode()).decode().split(\":\")\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n    payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}\"\n    good = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n    if not hmac.compare_digest(good, sig) or time.time() - int(ts) > max_age:\n        return None\n    return user_id\n\n\n# --- Intervals.icu calls ----------------------------------------------------\ndef post_form(url, fields):\n    data = urllib.parse.urlencode(fields).encode()\n    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\"Accept\": \"application/json\"})\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n        return json.loads(r.read().decode())\n\n\ndef exchange_code(code):\n    return post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\", \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID,\n        \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n    })\n\n\ndef store_connection(user_id, tok):\n    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n    athlete = tok.get(\"athlete\") or {}\n    with LOCK:\n        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\n            \"athlete_id\": athlete.get(\"id\"), \"athlete_name\": athlete.get(\"name\"),\n            \"access_token\": tok[\"access_token\"], \"refresh_token\": refresh,\n            \"scope\": tok.get(\"scope\"), \"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in, \"status\": \"connected\",\n        }\n    log(f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')} (expires in {expires_in}s)\")\n\n\ndef refresh_tokens():\n    \"\"\"Background pass: renew access tokens shortly before they expire.\"\"\"\n    while True:\n        time.sleep(config.REFRESH_INTERVAL)\n        now = time.time()\n        with LOCK:\n            for uid, c in CONNECTIONS.items():\n                if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:\n                    continue\n                if not c[\"refresh_token\"]:\n                    log(f\"{uid}: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\")\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    tok = post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n                        \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"refresh_token\": c[\"refresh_token\"],\n                        \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET,\n                    })\n                    c.update(access_token=tok[\"access_token\"],\n                             refresh_token=tok.get(\"refresh_token\", c[\"refresh_token\"]),\n                             expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))\n                    log(f\"{uid}: token refreshed\")\n                except Exception as e:\n                    log(f\"{uid}: refresh failed ({e}) -> expired, reconnect\")\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n\n\ndef intervals_get(conn, path):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{config.INTERVALS_BASE}/api/v1/athlete/{conn['athlete_id']}{path}\",\n                                 headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + conn[\"access_token\"]})\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n        return r.status, json.loads(r.read().decode())\n\n\n# --- HTTP ---------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, fmt, *args):\n        print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[http]\", fmt % args, flush=True)\n\n    def send_json(self, code, obj):\n        body = json.dumps(obj).encode()\n        self.send_response(code)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n        self.end_headers()\n        self.wfile.write(body)\n\n    def send_file(self, name, ctype):\n        p = os.path.join(STATIC, name)\n        if not os.path.isfile(p):\n            return self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n        with open(p, \"rb\") as f:\n            body = f.read()\n        self.send_response(200)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", ctype)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n        self.end_headers()\n        self.wfile.write(body)\n\n    def redirect(self, url):\n        self.send_response(302)\n        self.send_header(\"Location\", url)\n        self.end_headers()\n\n    def current_user(self):\n        auth = self.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n        if not auth.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n            return None\n        return USERS.get(auth[7:].strip())\n\n    def require_user(self):\n        user = self.current_user()\n        if user is None:\n            self.log_message(\"%s %s 401 (no Authorization header)\", self.command, self.path)\n            self.send_json(401, {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"})\n        return user\n\n    def do_GET(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n        q = dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(url.query))\n        if url.path == \"/\":\n            return self.send_file(\"index.html\", \"text/html; charset=utf-8\")\n        if url.path.startswith(\"/static/\"):\n            return self.send_file(os.path.basename(url.path), \"application/javascript\" if url.path.endswith(\".js\") else \"text/plain\")\n        if url.path == \"/api/me\":\n            user = self.require_user()\n            return user and self.send_json(200, user)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/callback\":\n            return self.callback(q)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/status\":\n            return self.status()\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/wellness\":\n            return self.wellness()\n        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n\n    def do_POST(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":\n            user = self.require_user()\n            if user:\n                with LOCK:\n                    CONNECTIONS.pop(user[\"id\"], None)\n                self.send_json(200, {\"ok\": True})\n            return\n        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n\n    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\n    def auth_init(self):\n        user = self.require_user()\n        if not user:\n            return\n        params = {\"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n                  \"scope\": config.SCOPES, \"state\": sign_state(user[\"id\"])}\n        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))\n\n    # Step 2: Intervals redirects back here with ?code=&state=.\n    def callback(self, q):\n        user_id = verify_state(q.get(\"state\", \"\"))\n        if not user_id or not q.get(\"code\"):\n            return self.send_json(400, {\"error\": \"bad state or code\"})\n        try:\n            tok = exchange_code(q[\"code\"])\n            store_connection(user_id, tok)\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: HTTP {e.code} {e.read()[:200]!r}\")\n            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n        except Exception as e:\n            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: {e}\")\n            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n        self.redirect(\"/?connected=1\")\n\n    def status(self):\n        user = self.require_user()\n        if not user:\n            return\n        with LOCK:\n            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n            return self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": False, \"status\": c[\"status\"] if c else \"disconnected\"})\n        self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": True, \"status\": \"connected\", \"scope\": c[\"scope\"],\n                             \"athlete\": {\"id\": c[\"athlete_id\"], \"name\": c[\"athlete_name\"]}})\n\n    def wellness(self):\n        user = self.require_user()\n        if not user:\n            return\n        with LOCK:\n            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n            return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n        try:\n            code, data = intervals_get(c, \"/wellness\")\n            self.send_json(code, data)\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})\n        except Exception as e:\n            self.send_json(502, {\"error\": str(e)})\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    threading.Thread(target=refresh_tokens, daemon=True).start()\n    log(f\"serving on http://localhost:{config.PORT} (intervals: {config.INTERVALS_BASE})\")\n    ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", config.PORT), Handler).serve_forever()\n// tricoach SPA. The sign-in token lives in localStorage and travels on every\n// API call via the fetch wrapper below.\nconst TOKEN = localStorage.getItem(\"tc_token\") || \"tok-okafor\";\nconst root = document.getElementById(\"app\");\n\nasync function api(path, opts = {}) {\n  const headers = Object.assign({ \"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN }, opts.headers || {});\n  const res = await fetch(path, Object.assign({}, opts, { headers }));\n  const body = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(body.error || (\"HTTP \" + res.status));\n  return body;\n}\n\nfunction esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g, c => ({ \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\" }[c])); }\n\nasync function render() {\n  try {\n    const me = await api(\"/api/me\");\n    const st = await api(\"/api/intervals/status\");\n    let card;\n    if (st.connected) {\n      card = `<div class=\"card\">Connected to Intervals.icu as <b>${esc(st.athlete.name)}</b>\n        (${esc(st.athlete.id)}), scope <code>${esc(st.scope)}</code>.\n        <p><button class=\"btn\" id=\"disconnect\">Disconnect</button></p></div>`;\n    } else {\n      const why = st.status && st.status !== \"disconnected\" ? `<p class=\"muted\">Status: ${esc(st.status)}</p>` : \"\";\n      card = `<div class=\"card\">Intervals.icu is not connected.${why}\n        <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a></p></div>`;\n    }\n    root.className = \"\";\n    root.innerHTML = `<p>Signed in as <b>${esc(me.name)}</b>.</p>${card}`;\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");\n    if (d) d.onclick = async () => { await api(\"/api/intervals/disconnect\", { method: \"POST\" }); render(); };\n  } catch (e) {\n    root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`;\n  }\n}\n\nrender();\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>tricoach</title>\n<style>\n  body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 42rem; padding: 0 1rem; }\n  .btn { display: inline-block; padding: .5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; background: #1d4ed8; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; border: 0; cursor: pointer; }\n  .card { border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }\n  .muted { color: #666; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>tricoach</h1>\n<div id=\"app\" class=\"muted\">Loading…</div>\n<script src=\"/static/app.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n---\ntitle: Intervals.icu OAuth quirks — no refresh_token, \"Duplicate scope\", and why the init endpoint must be POST\ndate: 2026-04-15\ntags: [intervals-icu, oauth, api-integration, web-auth, triathlon]\ntype: success\nstatus: n/a\nreproducible: true\n---\n\n# Intervals.icu OAuth quirks — no refresh_token, \"Duplicate scope\", and why the init endpoint must be POST\n\nI migrated my multi-tenant triathlon agent from per-user API keys to\nIntervals.icu OAuth, so athletes connect their account with two clicks\ninstead of pasting a key. Intervals' OAuth mostly follows the standard\nauthorization-code flow — but four deviations cost me real debugging time,\nand none of them are documented in one place.\n\n**1. The token never expires and never refreshes.** The token response has\nno `refresh_token` and no `expires_in` — the access token lives until the\nathlete revokes it in the Intervals UI. Upside: no refresh machinery at all.\nDownside: you can't know it's dead until it is. Handle revocation lazily —\non the first 401 from the API, clear the stored token and surface a\n\"reconnect\" prompt. And treat it as a perpetual credential: encrypt at rest.\n\n**2. `\"Duplicate scope\"`.** `:WRITE` implies `:READ`, and naming the same\narea twice — say `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE`, the natural habit from\nother providers — errors out with `Duplicate scope`. Each area at most once:\nmine is `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE,SETTINGS:WRITE`.\n\n**3. The token exchange is standard-lite.** `POST /api/oauth/token` wants\nonly `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code` — no `grant_type`, no\n`redirect_uri` echo. And the response bundles `athlete: {id, name}`, which\nsaves you the \"who am I\" round-trip; you need that athlete id in every API\npath anyway.\n\n**4. The self-inflicted one, fixed the same day.** I shipped the init\nendpoint as GET: a plain `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">` link that\nwould build the authorize URL and redirect. It 401'd for every single user —\na full-page navigation does **not** send the `Authorization` header your SPA\nkeeps in localStorage; headers only travel on XHR/fetch. Same-day rewrite:\ninit is an authenticated **POST** returning `{authorize_url}` as JSON, and\nthe frontend does `window.location.assign(authorize_url)`.\n\nWhich raises the follow-up: the *callback* arrives with no auth header\neither (it's a redirect from Intervals). So the `state` parameter carries\nthe identity — a signed JWT with the user id, a `purpose` claim, and a\n15-minute TTL, validated before the code exchange. On reconnect, an\naccount-mismatch guard rejects the callback if the incoming athlete id\ndiffers from the one already stored.\n\n## Reproduce this\n\nPrerequisites: a web app with its own user auth where the API token travels\nin an `Authorization` header (localStorage + fetch wrapper or similar); an\nIntervals.icu OAuth client — registration is arranged through the\n[Intervals.icu API access thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609)\n(you get a `client_id` / `client_secret` and register your `redirect_uri`).\nNo special agent skills required — this is ordinary backend + SPA work.\n\nYour agent will need from you: your OAuth `client_id` and `client_secret`,\nthe `redirect_uri` you registered, and where your app keeps its JWT signing\nsecret and per-user encrypted storage.\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Init endpoint: authenticated `POST /auth/init` (XHR, not a link). Build\n   `https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=...&redirect_uri=...&scope=...&state=...`\n   and return it as JSON `{authorize_url}`; the frontend calls\n   `window.location.assign(authorize_url)`. Do not make this a GET — the\n   full-page navigation drops your auth header.\n2. Scope string: list each area once, `:WRITE` where you write, `:READ` only\n   for areas you never write — never both for the same area.\n3. `state`: a signed JWT `{sub: user_id, purpose: \"intervals_oauth\", exp:\n   now+15min}` — the callback has no other way to know which of your users\n   it belongs to.\n4. Callback endpoint (`GET`, unauthenticated): validate `state` signature,\n   TTL, and purpose; then `POST https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token` with\n   form fields `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code` only. From the JSON\n   response take `access_token`, `scope`, and `athlete.id`; store the token\n   encrypted. Do not wait for a `refresh_token` — there isn't one.\n5. API client: send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` against\n   `https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/{athlete_id}/...`. On a 401, clear\n   the stored token and mark the user as disconnected.\n\nVerify: complete the flow with a real Intervals.icu account, then\n`GET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/wellness` with the Bearer token — it must return\ndata. Revoke the app in Intervals.icu settings and repeat the call — it must\n401, and your app must degrade to \"reconnect\" instead of crashing. Finally,\nrequest a scope with a duplicated area on the authorize URL — Intervals\nmust reject it with the `Duplicate scope` error, confirming rule 2.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8be47a90-2f7b-4aee-aba8-b973aef40035","uuid":"83287278-cef3-4484-b12c-b2c3de1bbfd5","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:48:41.196Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# tricoach\n\nBackend + single-page app for a small triathlon coaching practice. Coaches\nplan the week; athletes see it and connect their Intervals.icu account so the\napp can read wellness data and push planned workouts to their calendar. The\nathlete signs in to tricoach (token in `localStorage`, sent as\n`Authorization: Bearer` by the SPA's fetch wrapper), then clicks\n\"Connect Intervals.icu\", which runs the OAuth flow against Intervals.\n\n`server.py` is stdlib only (`python3 server.py`, port 8766) and keeps\neverything in memory; the shape is the same as the Postgres tables in prod.\nDev sign-in tokens: `tok-okafor` (default in the SPA) and `tok-rivera`.\n`config.py` holds the OAuth client placeholders. `logs/` has what we captured\nwhile looking into the connection problems.\nimport os\n\nPORT = 8766\nAPP_SECRET = \"dev-only-change-me-7c1f0a\"          # signs the OAuth state parameter\n\n# Intervals.icu OAuth client (placeholders; the real pair is in the deploy env)\nINTERVALS_BASE = os.environ.get(\"INTERVALS_BASE\", \"https://intervals.icu\")\nCLIENT_ID = \"tricoach-dev\"\nCLIENT_SECRET = \"s3cr3t-placeholder-0000\"\nREDIRECT_URI = f\"http://localhost:{PORT}/api/intervals/callback\"\nSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"\n\nREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"tricoach backend: sign-in, Intervals.icu OAuth connection, wellness proxy.\n\nStdlib only. State is in memory (same shape as the prod tables).\n\"\"\"\nimport base64, hashlib, hmac, json, os, threading, time\nimport urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n\nimport config\n\nSTATIC = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \"static\")\nTOKEN_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/api/oauth/token\"\nAUTHORIZE_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/oauth/authorize\"\nDEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n\n# --- in-memory store -------------------------------------------------------\nUSERS = {\n    \"tok-okafor\": {\"id\": \"u_okafor\", \"name\": \"C. Okafor\"},\n    \"tok-rivera\": {\"id\": \"u_rivera\", \"name\": \"T. Rivera\"},\n}\n# user_id -> {athlete_id, athlete_name, access_token, refresh_token, scope, expires_at, status}\nCONNECTIONS = {}\nLOCK = threading.Lock()\n\n\ndef log(msg):\n    print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[intervals]\", msg, flush=True)\n\n\n# --- state parameter: carries the user through the redirect -----------------\ndef sign_state(user_id):\n    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}\"\n    sig = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(f\"{payload}:{sig}\".encode()).decode()\n\n\ndef verify_state(state, max_age=900):\n    try:\n        user_id, ts, sig = base64.urlsafe_b64decode(state.encode()).decode().split(\":\")\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n    payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}\"\n    good = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n    if not hmac.compare_digest(good, sig) or time.time() - int(ts) > max_age:\n        return None\n    return user_id\n\n\n# --- Intervals.icu calls ----------------------------------------------------\ndef post_form(url, fields):\n    data = urllib.parse.urlencode(fields).encode()\n    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\"Accept\": \"application/json\"})\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n        return json.loads(r.read().decode())\n\n\ndef exchange_code(code):\n    return post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\", \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID,\n        \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n    })\n\n\ndef store_connection(user_id, tok):\n    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n    athlete = tok.get(\"athlete\") or {}\n    with LOCK:\n        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\n            \"athlete_id\": athlete.get(\"id\"), \"athlete_name\": athlete.get(\"name\"),\n            \"access_token\": tok[\"access_token\"], \"refresh_token\": refresh,\n            \"scope\": tok.get(\"scope\"), \"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in, \"status\": \"connected\",\n        }\n    log(f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')} (expires in {expires_in}s)\")\n\n\ndef refresh_tokens():\n    \"\"\"Background pass: renew access tokens shortly before they expire.\"\"\"\n    while True:\n        time.sleep(config.REFRESH_INTERVAL)\n        now = time.time()\n        with LOCK:\n            for uid, c in CONNECTIONS.items():\n                if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:\n                    continue\n                if not c[\"refresh_token\"]:\n                    log(f\"{uid}: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\")\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    tok = post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n                        \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"refresh_token\": c[\"refresh_token\"],\n                        \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET,\n                    })\n                    c.update(access_token=tok[\"access_token\"],\n                             refresh_token=tok.get(\"refresh_token\", c[\"refresh_token\"]),\n                             expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))\n                    log(f\"{uid}: token refreshed\")\n                except Exception as e:\n                    log(f\"{uid}: refresh failed ({e}) -> expired, reconnect\")\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n\n\ndef intervals_get(conn, path):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{config.INTERVALS_BASE}/api/v1/athlete/{conn['athlete_id']}{path}\",\n                                 headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + conn[\"access_token\"]})\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n        return r.status, json.loads(r.read().decode())\n\n\n# --- HTTP ---------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, fmt, *args):\n        print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[http]\", fmt % args, flush=True)\n\n    def send_json(self, code, obj):\n        body = json.dumps(obj).encode()\n        self.send_response(code)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n        self.end_headers()\n        self.wfile.write(body)\n\n    def send_file(self, name, ctype):\n        p = os.path.join(STATIC, name)\n        if not os.path.isfile(p):\n            return self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n        with open(p, \"rb\") as f:\n            body = f.read()\n        self.send_response(200)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", ctype)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n        self.end_headers()\n        self.wfile.write(body)\n\n    def redirect(self, url):\n        self.send_response(302)\n        self.send_header(\"Location\", url)\n        self.end_headers()\n\n    def current_user(self):\n        auth = self.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n        if not auth.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n            return None\n        return USERS.get(auth[7:].strip())\n\n    def require_user(self):\n        user = self.current_user()\n        if user is None:\n            self.log_message(\"%s %s 401 (no Authorization header)\", self.command, self.path)\n            self.send_json(401, {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"})\n        return user\n\n    def do_GET(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n        q = dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(url.query))\n        if url.path == \"/\":\n            return self.send_file(\"index.html\", \"text/html; charset=utf-8\")\n        if url.path.startswith(\"/static/\"):\n            return self.send_file(os.path.basename(url.path), \"application/javascript\" if url.path.endswith(\".js\") else \"text/plain\")\n        if url.path == \"/api/me\":\n            user = self.require_user()\n            return user and self.send_json(200, user)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/callback\":\n            return self.callback(q)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/status\":\n            return self.status()\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/wellness\":\n            return self.wellness()\n        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n\n    def do_POST(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":\n            user = self.require_user()\n            if user:\n                with LOCK:\n                    CONNECTIONS.pop(user[\"id\"], None)\n                self.send_json(200, {\"ok\": True})\n            return\n        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n\n    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\n    def auth_init(self):\n        user = self.require_user()\n        if not user:\n            return\n        params = {\"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n                  \"scope\": config.SCOPES, \"state\": sign_state(user[\"id\"])}\n        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))\n\n    # Step 2: Intervals redirects back here with ?code=&state=.\n    def callback(self, q):\n        user_id = verify_state(q.get(\"state\", \"\"))\n        if not user_id or not q.get(\"code\"):\n            return self.send_json(400, {\"error\": \"bad state or code\"})\n        try:\n            tok = exchange_code(q[\"code\"])\n            store_connection(user_id, tok)\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: HTTP {e.code} {e.read()[:200]!r}\")\n            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n        except Exception as e:\n            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: {e}\")\n            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n        self.redirect(\"/?connected=1\")\n\n    def status(self):\n        user = self.require_user()\n        if not user:\n            return\n        with LOCK:\n            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n            return self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": False, \"status\": c[\"status\"] if c else \"disconnected\"})\n        self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": True, \"status\": \"connected\", \"scope\": c[\"scope\"],\n                             \"athlete\": {\"id\": c[\"athlete_id\"], \"name\": c[\"athlete_name\"]}})\n\n    def wellness(self):\n        user = self.require_user()\n        if not user:\n            return\n        with LOCK:\n            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n            return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n        try:\n            code, data = intervals_get(c, \"/wellness\")\n            self.send_json(code, data)\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})\n        except Exception as e:\n            self.send_json(502, {\"error\": str(e)})\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    threading.Thread(target=refresh_tokens, daemon=True).start()\n    log(f\"serving on http://localhost:{config.PORT} (intervals: {config.INTERVALS_BASE})\")\n    ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", config.PORT), Handler).serve_forever()\n// tricoach SPA. The sign-in token lives in localStorage and travels on every\n// API call via the fetch wrapper below.\nconst TOKEN = localStorage.getItem(\"tc_token\") || \"tok-okafor\";\nconst root = document.getElementById(\"app\");\n\nasync function api(path, opts = {}) {\n  const headers = Object.assign({ \"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN }, opts.headers || {});\n  const res = await fetch(path, Object.assign({}, opts, { headers }));\n  const body = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(body.error || (\"HTTP \" + res.status));\n  return body;\n}\n\nfunction esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g, c => ({ \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\" }[c])); }\n\nasync function render() {\n  try {\n    const me = await api(\"/api/me\");\n    const st = await api(\"/api/intervals/status\");\n    let card;\n    if (st.connected) {\n      card = `<div class=\"card\">Connected to Intervals.icu as <b>${esc(st.athlete.name)}</b>\n        (${esc(st.athlete.id)}), scope <code>${esc(st.scope)}</code>.\n        <p><button class=\"btn\" id=\"disconnect\">Disconnect</button></p></div>`;\n    } else {\n      const why = st.status && st.status !== \"disconnected\" ? `<p class=\"muted\">Status: ${esc(st.status)}</p>` : \"\";\n      card = `<div class=\"card\">Intervals.icu is not connected.${why}\n        <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a></p></div>`;\n    }\n    root.className = \"\";\n    root.innerHTML = `<p>Signed in as <b>${esc(me.name)}</b>.</p>${card}`;\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");\n    if (d) d.onclick = async () => { await api(\"/api/intervals/disconnect\", { method: \"POST\" }); render(); };\n  } catch (e) {\n    root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`;\n  }\n}\n\nrender();\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>tricoach</title>\n<style>\n  body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 42rem; padding: 0 1rem; }\n  .btn { display: inline-block; padding: .5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; background: #1d4ed8; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; border: 0; cursor: pointer; }\n  .card { border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }\n  .muted { color: #666; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>tricoach</h1>\n<div id=\"app\" class=\"muted\">Loading…</div>\n<script src=\"/static/app.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n---\ntitle: Intervals.icu OAuth quirks — no refresh_token, \"Duplicate scope\", and why the init endpoint must be POST\ndate: 2026-04-15\ntags: [intervals-icu, oauth, api-integration, web-auth, triathlon]\ntype: success\nstatus: n/a\nreproducible: true\n---\n\n# Intervals.icu OAuth quirks — no refresh_token, \"Duplicate scope\", and why the init endpoint must be POST\n\nI migrated my multi-tenant triathlon agent from per-user API keys to\nIntervals.icu OAuth, so athletes connect their account with two clicks\ninstead of pasting a key. Intervals' OAuth mostly follows the standard\nauthorization-code flow — but four deviations cost me real debugging time,\nand none of them are documented in one place.\n\n**1. The token never expires and never refreshes.** The token response has\nno `refresh_token` and no `expires_in` — the access token lives until the\nathlete revokes it in the Intervals UI. Upside: no refresh machinery at all.\nDownside: you can't know it's dead until it is. Handle revocation lazily —\non the first 401 from the API, clear the stored token and surface a\n\"reconnect\" prompt. And treat it as a perpetual credential: encrypt at rest.\n\n**2. `\"Duplicate scope\"`.** `:WRITE` implies `:READ`, and naming the same\narea twice — say `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE`, the natural habit from\nother providers — errors out with `Duplicate scope`. Each area at most once:\nmine is `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE,SETTINGS:WRITE`.\n\n**3. The token exchange is standard-lite.** `POST /api/oauth/token` wants\nonly `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code` — no `grant_type`, no\n`redirect_uri` echo. And the response bundles `athlete: {id, name}`, which\nsaves you the \"who am I\" round-trip; you need that athlete id in every API\npath anyway.\n\n**4. The self-inflicted one, fixed the same day.** I shipped the init\nendpoint as GET: a plain `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">` link that\nwould build the authorize URL and redirect. It 401'd for every single user —\na full-page navigation does **not** send the `Authorization` header your SPA\nkeeps in localStorage; headers only travel on XHR/fetch. Same-day rewrite:\ninit is an authenticated **POST** returning `{authorize_url}` as JSON, and\nthe frontend does `window.location.assign(authorize_url)`.\n\nWhich raises the follow-up: the *callback* arrives with no auth header\neither (it's a redirect from Intervals). So the `state` parameter carries\nthe identity — a signed JWT with the user id, a `purpose` claim, and a\n15-minute TTL, validated before the code exchange. On reconnect, an\naccount-mismatch guard rejects the callback if the incoming athlete id\ndiffers from the one already stored.\n\n## Reproduce this\n\nPrerequisites: a web app with its own user auth where the API token travels\nin an `Authorization` header (localStorage + fetch wrapper or similar); an\nIntervals.icu OAuth client — registration is arranged through the\n[Intervals.icu API access thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609)\n(you get a `client_id` / `client_secret` and register your `redirect_uri`).\nNo special agent skills required — this is ordinary backend + SPA work.\n\nYour agent will need from you: your OAuth `client_id` and `client_secret`,\nthe `redirect_uri` you registered, and where your app keeps its JWT signing\nsecret and per-user encrypted storage.\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Init endpoint: authenticated `POST /auth/init` (XHR, not a link). Build\n   `https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=...&redirect_uri=...&scope=...&state=...`\n   and return it as JSON `{authorize_url}`; the frontend calls\n   `window.location.assign(authorize_url)`. Do not make this a GET — the\n   full-page navigation drops your auth header.\n2. Scope string: list each area once, `:WRITE` where you write, `:READ` only\n   for areas you never write — never both for the same area.\n3. `state`: a signed JWT `{sub: user_id, purpose: \"intervals_oauth\", exp:\n   now+15min}` — the callback has no other way to know which of your users\n   it belongs to.\n4. Callback endpoint (`GET`, unauthenticated): validate `state` signature,\n   TTL, and purpose; then `POST https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token` with\n   form fields `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code` only. From the JSON\n   response take `access_token`, `scope`, and `athlete.id`; store the token\n   encrypted. Do not wait for a `refresh_token` — there isn't one.\n5. API client: send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` against\n   `https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/{athlete_id}/...`. On a 401, clear\n   the stored token and mark the user as disconnected.\n\nVerify: complete the flow with a real Intervals.icu account, then\n`GET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/wellness` with the Bearer token — it must return\ndata. Revoke the app in Intervals.icu settings and repeat the call — it must\n401, and your app must degrade to \"reconnect\" instead of crashing. Finally,\nrequest a scope with a duplicated area on the authorize URL — Intervals\nmust reject it with the `Duplicate scope` error, confirming rule 2.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UKvcvyUdqFvJYLGJatcvH8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
